%description:

Tcp.fastopenKey:random -- the cookie comes from a key of the RNG, and it brings in the data of the next SYN.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "TCP Fast Open, server: the key of the cookies, in the format of Linux
net.ipv4.tcp_fastopen_key ...; a cookie of 8 bytes is then the cookie of Linux with this key;
empty: a key from the RNG".

The classes: random ("", the default: a key from the RNG), fixed (a key of Linux: the cookie of
8 bytes is that of Linux), invalid (another format: an error at the first cookie), and changed
(the parameter is @mutable: a new key refuses the cookies of the old one). The code:
Tcp::generateFastOpenCookie() reads the key at each cookie that it makes or checks. The cookie
of Linux comes from a Linux run of the packetdrill script fastopen/server/simple1.pkt (inet-gpl):
the key a0bf63f7-ed803d81-cd641d30-cebc4a90 gives the client 10.248.0.2 at the server
192.168.0.2 the cookie 00abaaabe8e954c2 (the script sets these addresses itself). This test separates "random" from "fixed".

Host under test: host2, a Fast Open server; host1 is a Fast Open client (preconditions). host1
has the address 10.248.0.2 and host2 192.168.0.2, as in the Linux run, with the router between
them. host1 opens connection 1 at 0.1 s with Fast Open, which requests a cookie; at 0.5 s it opens
connection 2 with Fast Open and sends 500 bytes, which go on the SYN when host1 has a cookie
of host2. Observation: level 1, the cookie of connection 1 has 8 bytes and is not the cookie of the
Linux key; the SYN-ACK of connection 2 acknowledges its 500 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenKey
%# class: random
%# value: ""
%# key: *.host2.tcp.fastopenKey
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpFastopenKeyRandom")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 1 with Fast Open"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie == "";
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 1: a cookie request")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie.size() == 16 && cookie != "00abaaabe8e954c2";
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN-ACK of connection 1: a cookie of 8 bytes, not that of the Linux key")
                  .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(0.5).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[1]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); app.sendData(app.socket(), 500); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 2 with Fast Open, and sends 500 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .capture("isn2", "tcp.sequenceNo")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie.size() == 16;
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 2, with 500 bytes and the cookie")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn2} + 501")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of connection 2 acknowledges the SYN and the 500 bytes")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenKeyRandom compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.fastopenKey = ""    # the parameter under test
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
*.configurator.config = xml("<config><interface hosts='host1' names='eth0' address='10.248.0.2' netmask='255.255.255.0'/><interface hosts='router' names='eth0' address='10.248.0.1' netmask='255.255.255.0'/><interface hosts='router' names='eth1' address='192.168.0.1' netmask='255.255.255.0'/><interface hosts='host2' names='eth0' address='192.168.0.2' netmask='255.255.255.0'/></config>")
*.host2.tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = true
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.host1.numApps = 2
*.host1.app[*].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpFastopenKeyRandom: PASS
